<div class="wrap">
  <header class="head">
    <span class="logo-badge"><img src="assets/hal-logo.png" alt="Heung A Line"></span>
    <div class="tag">MMAN EDI file tool · Import customs declaration</div>
    <h1>Change Status → MMAN</h1>
    <p class="lede">Fills in POL, SHED NO. and country code, and changes the container STATUS in the MMAN file from the job's B/L list. You get MMAN_EDI.txt with every line the same length as before, ready to send on.</p>
    <div class="flow" aria-label="Workflow">
      <span class="doc">MMAN_*.txt</span><span class="op">+</span>
      <span class="doc">SUR.xls</span><span class="op">→</span>
      <span class="out">MMAN_EDI.txt</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="../#change-status">Use online (no install)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Rattanao/Change-status-mman/archive/refs/heads/main.zip">Download the program (ZIP)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Rattanao/Change-status-mman">Open on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="panel" id="online">
    <h2>Use online</h2>
    <p class="sub">Fastest, nothing to install. Files are processed in your browser only and are never uploaded to a server.</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><div><p><b>Open the <a href="../#change-status">online tool</a></b> and choose the MMAN file (.txt)</p></div></li>
      <li><div><p><b>Choose the STATUS list</b> (.xls / .xlsx / .csv)</p></div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Start B/L … End B/L</b> (only if you want to cut the file)</p>
        <p class="note">Keeps the PSKV line, then keeps only the B/Ls in this range (including sub-B/Ls …A, …B and their container lines); everything else is cut · Start left empty = from the first B/L · End left empty = to the last line · Both empty = no cut</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Check SHED NO.</b> Left box = B/Ls that have a Status, right box = all other B/Ls</p>
        <p class="note">Defaults <code>0145</code> / <code>0122</code>, change them to suit the job · <b>Jobs with no Status (e.g. LCH)</b>: enter SHED NO. in the left box and clear the right box = the same value for every B/L</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Click Change</b>, review the summary, then click <b>Download MMAN_EDI.txt</b></p>
        <p class="note">The file is saved to your Downloads folder · If the page still looks old, press <code>Ctrl + F5</code></p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="install">
    <h2>First-time setup (desktop program)</h2>
    <p class="sub">Once per computer, Windows · If you only use the online tool, skip this section</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Install Python 3</b> from <a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">python.org/downloads</a></p>
        <p class="note">On the installer's first screen <span class="warn">tick ☑ Add python.exe to PATH</span> before clicking Install Now</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Download the program</b> with the “Download the program (ZIP)” button above</p>
        <p class="note">Right-click the ZIP → Extract All, and keep the folder anywhere, e.g. Documents</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>The first run needs an internet connection</b></p>
        <p class="note">The program installs the libraries it needs (pandas, xlrd, openpyxl) automatically</p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="use">
    <h2>Every job</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Put the files in the <code>input</code> folder</b></p>
        <p class="note">Remove the previous job's files first, then add one MMAN file (.txt) and one STATUS list (.xls/.xlsx/.csv). An old MMAN_EDI.txt left there is not counted as a source file</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Double-click <code>run-change-status.bat</code></b></p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Type the SHED NO.</b> and press Enter twice</p>
        <p class="note">It asks for two values: B/Ls with a Status and all other B/Ls. Press Enter to skip and use <code>0145</code> and <code>0122</code> · Type <code>=</code> for the second value = use the first value for every B/L (LCH jobs)</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Open the result at <code>output\MMAN_EDI.txt</code></b></p>
        <p class="note">The black window summarises the number of B/Ls, Status changes and PG→PX. If you see a <code>WARNING</code> line, read it before using the file</p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="list">
    <h2>STATUS list (Excel)</h2>
    <p class="sub">Only columns A–C are used, with the header in the first row; ignore columns D–F. The program finds the columns by their header names, so both forms work</p>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h3>SUR form</h3>
        <div class="sheet-scroll">
          <table class="sheet">
            <thead><tr><th class="col">A</th><th class="col">B</th><th class="col">C</th></tr>
              <tr><th>POL</th><th>Status</th><th>B/L No.</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>CNSHA</td><td class="y">7  N</td><td>HASLC…909702</td></tr>
              <tr><td>CNSHA</td><td></td><td>HASLC…909850</td></tr>
              <tr><td>KRPTK</td><td></td><td>HASLK…804417</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>KMBK form</h3>
        <div class="sheet-scroll">
          <table class="sheet">
            <thead><tr><th class="col">A</th><th class="col">B</th><th class="col">C</th></tr>
              <tr><th>B/L No.</th><th>Status</th><th>POL</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>HASLK…700462</td><td class="y">9  N</td><td>KRPUS</td></tr>
              <tr><td>HASLK…805808</td><td></td><td>KRPUS</td></tr>
              <tr><td>HASLK…807609</td><td></td><td>KRKAN</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Illustration only, B/L numbers shortened</p>
    <ul class="check-list">
      <li><b>B/L No.</b>: the master B/L number, which also covers its sub-B/Ls (…462A, …462B)</li>
      <li><b>Status</b>: e.g. <code>9  N</code>, <code>7  N</code>; any number of spaces works (<code>7 N</code>, <code>7N</code>), the program puts it in the right position · Empty = keep the original Status</li>
      <li><b>POL</b>: 5 letters, e.g. <code>KRPUS</code>, <code>CNSHA</code></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="changes">
    <h2>What changes in the MMAN file</h2>
    <p class="sub">Only the defined positions are edited; file size and line endings stay identical byte for byte</p>
    <div class="line-scroll">
<pre class="mline"><span class="lab">Before</span>HASLK01260700462                             THBKK    GOLDWAY…   TH   …   O ACRYLONITRILE…
<span class="lab">After</span>HASLK01260700462                   <mark class="b">KRPUS</mark><mark class="g">THBKK</mark>THBKK<mark class="o">0145</mark>GOLDWAY…   <mark class="b">KR</mark>   …   O ACRYLONITRILE…
<span class="lab">Before</span>SKHU9545854      8  N   1        Y
<span class="lab">After</span>SKHU9545854      <mark class="y">9</mark>  N   1        Y</pre>
    </div>
    <div class="trouble-scroll">
      <table class="rules">
        <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Position</th><th>Value written</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="chip b">1</span></td><td class="pos">col 36–40</td><td>POL from the list, e.g. KRPUS</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip g">2</span></td><td class="pos">col 41–45</td><td>The port of most B/Ls in the file (THBKK or THLCH), e.g. CNTAO<b>THLCH</b>THLKR0332</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip">3</span></td><td class="pos">col 46–50</td><td>Port as in the original (THBKK, THLCH, THLKR, …), not changed</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip o">4</span></td><td class="pos">col 51–54</td><td>SHED NO., locked by the original port: <b>BMT 0110 · SCT 0302 · LKR 0332 · UCT 0113 · LCH with DG (has UN/CLASS) 2826 · BKK going to LAOS 0124</b> · Other BKK and LCH B/Ls use the SHED NO. boxes (<code>0145</code> if the B/L has a Status, <code>0122</code> for the rest · right box empty = use the left value)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip b">5</span></td><td class="pos">col 844–845</td><td>First 2 letters of the POL in place of TH (KR, CN)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip y">6</span></td><td class="pos">Container line</td><td>Status from the list, e.g. 8&nbsp;&nbsp;N → 9&nbsp;&nbsp;N</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip r">PX</span></td><td class="pos">Package unit</td><td>PG → PX on every B/L</td></tr>
<tr><td><span class="chip b">5</span></td><td class="pos">col 3804</td><td>Letter O before the description → <b>5 only for B/Ls with Status 9&nbsp;&nbsp;N</b> · other B/Ls keep O · except TRANSIT/TRANSHIPMENT, which use 7 / 3 / L</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip g">N</span></td><td class="pos">col 881 · 974 · 1765</td><td>Consignee name and notify name = always the notify name at <b>col 1672 (TH + name), single-spaced</b>, on every B/L (BKK and LCH) · The address after the name is kept · Except TRANSIT/TRANSHIPMENT, which are left unchanged</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip y">T</span></td><td class="pos">col 1670 · 3804</td><td><b>TRANSIT/TRANSHIPMENT</b>: the TH before the notify name = destination country (LA, MM, KH, CN, PG, MY) · Letter before the description: TRANSIT = 7, TRANSIT to LAOS = per CARGO MOVEMENT (L / 7), TRANSHIPMENT = 3</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="chip">−</span></td><td class="pos">col 1742 · 1416 · 2207</td><td>Every B/L except TRANSIT/TRANSHIPMENT: clears the notify tax ID and the consignee / notify addresses (the consignee tax ID and branch code are kept)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h3>Always kept</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>The letter <code>O</code> before the description (except TRANSIT/TRANSHIPMENT)</li>
          <li>Names on TRANSIT/TRANSHIPMENT B/Ls</li>
          <li>The Status of B/Ls whose Status cell is empty</li>
          <li>B/Ls not in the list (you get a warning)</li>
          <li>The source files in input are never edited</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Check the summary every time</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Number of B/Ls changed matches the list</li>
          <li>Number of SHED 0145 / 0122</li>
          <li>Status changes and number of container lines</li>
          <li>B/Ls changed PG → PX</li>
          <li>File size equals the original</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="claude">
    <h2>Use with Claude Code</h2>
    <p class="sub">For people who already use Claude Code: install the skill once, then ask with the words "Change status"</p>
    <div class="cmd">
      <pre id="clone">git clone https://github.com/Rattanao/Change-status-mman.git %TEMP%\csm &amp;&amp; xcopy /E /I /Y %TEMP%\csm\change-status %USERPROFILE%\.claude\skills\change-status</pre>
      <button type="button" data-target="clone">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Restart Claude Code, go to the job folder that has input, and type “Change status”</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="help">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <div class="trouble-scroll">
      <table class="trouble">
        <thead><tr><th>Message / symptom</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Python not found / Python was not found</td><td>Reinstall Python and tick Add python.exe to PATH</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ERROR: need exactly 1 MMAN .txt and 1 list file</td><td>input must hold exactly one MMAN file and one STATUS list; remove the previous job's files</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ERROR: no B/L in the MMAN file matches the list</td><td>The STATUS list is not for this vessel; check you paired the right files</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WARNING B/L NOT in list</td><td>B/Ls in the MMAN file that are not in the list are not changed; add them to the list and run again</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ERROR: unrecognised Status</td><td>A Status must be 1 digit + 1 letter, e.g. 9  N</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PermissionError: [Errno 13]</td><td>Close MMAN_EDI.txt if it is open, then run again</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Start B/L … not found / B/L … not found in the MMAN file</td><td>Type the B/L exactly as in the MMAN file (master B/L, without the A, B suffix); the End B/L must come after the Start B/L</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The page still looks old</td><td>Press Ctrl + F5</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p class="credit">Project by <b>Ms. Rattana Mudlae</b> · Position Import DOC.</p>
    <p>Check the summary every time before sending MMAN_EDI.txt, especially any WARNING lines</p>
    <p>Updating the program: download the ZIP again and extract over the old folder · Source code: <a href="https://github.com/Rattanao/Change-status-mman">github.com/Rattanao/Change-status-mman</a></p>
  </footer>
</div>
